<title>INDIA: Indian soybean market shut on traders' protest.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean market shut on traders' protest.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean markets were closed on Friday on traders' objection to an increase in taxes, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said soybean markets would remain closed indefinitely in protest against an increase in local taxes which came into effect on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
